From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 12:29:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] cpu/intel/haswell: Give macOS plugin-type on the first
 Processor object

With the CPU threads declared as Processor objects (acpi_cpu_objects),
macOS finds them, but its kernel runs XCPM, its CPU power management,
only when the first thread carries the property plugin-type 1, which
makes it load the X86PlatformPlugin. OpenCore configurations add it with
an SSDT, OpenCore's SSDT-PLUG sample, that defines _DSM on the first
CPU.

Add that _DSM to the first Processor object: for Apple's UUID
(a0b5b7c6-1318-441c-b0c9-fe695eaf949b) function 0 lists function 1,
which returns Package () { "plugin-type", 1 }; other functions and
other UUIDs get Buffer () { 0 }. No other OS asks with Apple's UUID.
The Device (ACPI0007) objects, the default, get no _DSM: macOS does not
find CPUs declared that way. An SSDT-PLUG still in the OpenCore
configuration cannot add its own _DSM to \_SB.CP00, which has one.

TEST=Built lenovo/w541 with mrc.bin and with the native RAM init. The
SSDT that acpigen writes for two threads, with acpigen.c built for the
host, loads in acpiexec 20230628: \_SB.CP00._DSM returns Buffer {0x03}
for function 0 of Apple's UUID, Package {"plugin-type", 1} for function
1, Buffer {0} for function 2 and for another UUID; CP01 has no _DSM.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 src/cpu/intel/haswell/acpi.c | 26 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/cpu/intel/haswell/cfr.h  |  7 +++++--
 2 files changed, 31 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/cpu/intel/haswell/acpi.c b/src/cpu/intel/haswell/acpi.c
index fd47320d13..3216bbb695 100644
--- a/src/cpu/intel/haswell/acpi.c
+++ b/src/cpu/intel/haswell/acpi.c
@@ -332,6 +332,25 @@ static void generate_P_state_entries(int core, int cores_per_package)
 	acpigen_pop_len();
 }
 
+/*
+ * The _DSM through which macOS takes device properties (Apple's UUID), on
+ * the first thread: plugin-type 1 there makes the kernel load the
+ * X86PlatformPlugin, thus XCPM, the CPU power management of macOS. It is
+ * what the SSDT-PLUG sample of OpenCore adds; no other OS asks with this
+ * UUID.
+ */
+#define APPLE_DSM_UUID	"a0b5b7c6-1318-441c-b0c9-fe695eaf949b"
+
+static void apple_dsm_plugin_type(void *arg)
+{
+	/* Return (Package () { "plugin-type", 1 }) */
+	acpigen_emit_byte(RETURN_OP);
+	acpigen_write_package(2);
+	acpigen_write_string("plugin-type");
+	acpigen_write_integer(1);
+	acpigen_write_package_end();
+}
+
 static void generate_cpu_entry(const struct device *device, int cpu, int core,
 			       int cores_per_package, bool processor_op)
 {
@@ -357,6 +376,13 @@ static void generate_cpu_entry(const struct device *device, int cpu, int core,
 	/* Generate T-state tables */
 	generate_T_state_entries(cpu, cores_per_package);
 
+	/* macOS only finds Processor objects: plugin-type with them */
+	if (processor_op && index == 0) {
+		/* Function 0 lists function 1, the properties */
+		void (*callbacks[])(void *) = { NULL, apple_dsm_plugin_type };
+		acpigen_write_dsm(APPLE_DSM_UUID, callbacks, ARRAY_SIZE(callbacks), NULL);
+	}
+
 	if (processor_op)
 		acpigen_write_processor_end();
 	else
diff --git a/src/cpu/intel/haswell/cfr.h b/src/cpu/intel/haswell/cfr.h
index a64a76621e..bf8cc7504d 100644
--- a/src/cpu/intel/haswell/cfr.h
+++ b/src/cpu/intel/haswell/cfr.h
@@ -58,8 +58,11 @@ static const struct sm_object acpi_cpu_objects = SM_DECLARE_ENUM({
 	.ui_helptext	= "How the ACPI tables declare the CPU threads: as Device\n"
 			  "objects with _HID ACPI0007, the form ACPI asks for since\n"
 			  "version 6.3, or as Processor objects, the older form and\n"
-			  "the only one macOS looks for. Linux and Windows work with\n"
-			  "both.",
+			  "the only one macOS looks for, with plugin-type for XCPM on\n"
+			  "the first thread under macOS. Linux and Windows work with\n"
+			  "both.\n"
+			  "Default: Device. Processor for macOS, without the SSDTs\n"
+			  "that declare Processor objects and plugin-type.",
 	.default_value	= ACPI_CPU_OBJECTS_DEVICE,
 	.values		= (const struct sm_enum_value[]) {
 				{ "Device (ACPI0007)",	ACPI_CPU_OBJECTS_DEVICE		},
-- 
